{#
  Serif display, type-led hero, asymmetric split when a photo exists.

  The signature is the overhang. A masthead runs wider than the columns
  beneath it, so the name here pushes out of the content measure into the
  right margin instead of sitting obediently inside it. That is the one
  memorable move; everything else stays disciplined.

  It overhangs, it does not crop. A business owner reading their own name cut
  off by the page edge sees a bug, not a decision — so the overhang is capped
  at the gutter and the page is held against sideways scroll.
#}
{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% block style %}
body{overflow-x:hidden}
.hero{padding:4.5rem 1.5rem 3rem;display:grid;gap:2.5rem;align-items:start}
@media(min-width:820px){.hero{grid-template-columns:5fr 7fr}}
h1{font-family:Georgia,'Iowan Old Style','Times New Roman',serif;
  font-size:clamp(3rem,11vw,7rem);letter-spacing:-.03em;line-height:.95;margin:0;
  margin-right:calc(-1 * clamp(0rem,5vw,7rem))}
.lede{max-width:34rem;margin-top:1.4rem;font-size:1.05rem;opacity:.8}
h2{font-size:.8rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.18em;
  padding-bottom:.6rem;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(127,127,127,.35);margin:0 0 1.4rem}
h3{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:1.35rem;margin:2rem 0 .8rem}
.item{border-bottom:1px dotted rgba(127,127,127,.3)}
.facts-grid{display:grid;gap:2.5rem}
@media(min-width:820px){.facts-grid{grid-template-columns:5fr 7fr}}
{% endblock %}
